      "writtenOn": "2021-09-13T22:11:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ruibin, I\u0027m not totally following your comment as it relates to this CL. The purpose of this CL is to keep the CL you linked from breaking things. If this CL, by itself, will unacceptably increase power usage, then the fix for that should go in this CL.\n\nIIUC, you\u0027re saying that we can still enter LPM (without auto toggle) if we only do it when CC is open. As I mentioned elsewhere, I\u0027m not super familiar with the requirements for LPM in the absence of auto toggle. If we\u0027re in LPM and not toggling, will the timing of exiting LPM (and resuming the PD task) allow us to respond to an attach in a compliant amount of time?",
      "parentUuid": "dfad549b_852b7dc8",
      "revId": "3d9a8a2fed7bed421a0bcb75e2f8c6038518d996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06827260_26e92395",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288462
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-14T10:06:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For it83xx/it8xxx2, the plug-in interrupt would wakeup pd task,  then task check the partner connection on cc pins. We can respond to an attach in a compliant amount of time. But the problem is that TCPMv2 can\u0027t toggle Rp/Rd in LPM state when tDRPTransition time is up. \n\nI understand that the revert CL (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3114705/2) causes ITE pd cc not toggling, and this CL want to fix it.\n\nAfter reviewing original CL (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3088161) again, I found that the changes violates type-c spec, and left a comment there.",
      "parentUuid": "93d2fd2c_124cdf4c",
      "revId": "3d9a8a2fed7bed421a0bcb75e2f8c6038518d996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
